{"id": "0bbd6e3b-ee07-4290-b729-a618ab216060", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Looking at the resources, I see an ALB, ASG, an Aurora PostgreSQL cluster with only a writer instance and no reader, an EFS filesystem with just a single mount target in one AZ, an S3 bucket, security groups, and a subnet group. The lack of a second EFS mount target stands out as a gap—it means no AZ redundancy for file storage even though EFS is designed to be multi-AZ.

